just enjoying the fruits of her labor.

00:12:51.604 --> 00:12:52.480
[chuckles] Yeah.

00:12:52.563 --> 00:12:53.982
You know when you're 25,

00:12:54.065 --> 00:12:56.818
think about what you wanted
and who you were with

00:12:56.901 --> 00:12:59.195
-versus like, now, what you--
-Oh, I know.

00:12:59.279 --> 00:13:00.697
-It's so crazy.
-It's so different.

00:13:00.780 --> 00:13:04.200
I mean, I wouldn't wanna be
with the person I was dating at 25.

00:13:04.284 --> 00:13:05.326
Oh, my God.

00:13:05.410 --> 00:13:09.414
I did not know who I was at 25...
and I didn't know what I wanted,

00:13:09.497 --> 00:13:13.543
because actually if I ended up
with the person I was with at 25,

00:13:13.626 --> 00:13:16.379
I would want to kill myself. [laughs]

00:13:17.880 --> 00:13:21.509
And, yeah, you can Google that.
You were a dick. [laughs]

00:13:22.552 --> 00:13:23.636
Sorry.

00:13:23.720 --> 00:13:25.138
Honestly, I don't know if it's fair

00:13:25.221 --> 00:13:27.765
to even ask someone at 25
if they want kids or not.

00:13:27.849 --> 00:13:29.600
He does want kids, I guess.

00:13:29.684 --> 00:13:33.313
-She's aware of it, you know?
-Oh, yeah, she can make her own decisions.

00:13:33.396 --> 00:13:35.940
So obviously I want Mary to be happy

00:13:36.024 --> 00:13:39.110
and I hope that this is
the right move for them.

00:13:39.193 --> 00:13:40.903
As somebody that is married,

00:13:40.987 --> 00:13:45.450
and I'm married to a wonderful person,
sometimes it's freaking hard.

00:13:45.533 --> 00:13:48.995
So I just hope that, 
you know, at 25 years old,

00:13:49.078 --> 00:13:52.915
he knows, you know, what that entails,
asking someone to marry you,

00:13:52.999 --> 00:13:55.460
because it's not always easy.

00:13:55.543 --> 00:13:58.212
Does Romain pay for his own share
of stuff, do you think?

00:13:58.296 --> 00:13:59.464
Not much, I think.

00:13:59.547 --> 00:14:00.882
So she pays for everything?

00:14:00.965 --> 00:14:03.885
Yeah. I mean, I don't know him super well.

00:14:03.968 --> 00:14:05.428
-I've heard he's a baker.
-Yeah.

00:14:05.511 --> 00:14:08.056
She's gonna do a prenup, right?

00:14:08.139 --> 00:14:10.892
I don't know. 
I haven't talked to her about it yet.

00:14:11.100 --> 00:14:13.227
-We can recommend it, but--
-I'm not gonna recommend it.

00:14:13.311 --> 00:14:14.812
-I won't recommend it either.
-[laughs]

00:14:14.896 --> 00:14:17.273
You know, she's obviously gonna do
what she wants to do.

00:14:17.357 --> 00:14:20.193
He's gonna do what he wants to do,
and hopefully that aligns.

00:14:20.276 --> 00:14:25.365
I mean, it's possible that it works out,
but it's risky, you know? [chuckles]

00:14:39.087 --> 00:14:41.422
[Heather] I'm so excited to see it. 
I cannot wait.

00:14:41.506 --> 00:14:44.008
-I hope that it's way better.
-[Brett] Oh, that makes two of us.

00:14:44.092 --> 00:14:44.967
[Heather] Yes!

00:14:45.259 --> 00:14:46.469
[gasps]

00:14:46.552 --> 00:14:48.554
Yes! I love it

00:14:50.598 --> 00:14:52.058
[Heather] I love the couch.

00:14:52.141 --> 00:14:54.143
It's white, exactly like what we wanted.

00:14:55.103 --> 00:14:56.479
So let's see the kitchen.

00:14:57.980 --> 00:14:59.565
Awesome. Simple.

00:15:00.233 --> 00:15:02.235
I didn't wanna take away
from the countertops.

00:15:02.318 --> 00:15:03.361
I feel like it's perfect.

00:15:03.778 --> 00:15:05.780
[Brett] No, it's clean, it's modern.

00:15:06.364 --> 00:15:08.574
I love the chandelier. That's perfect.

00:15:08.658 --> 00:15:10.535
It ties in that table so nice.

00:15:10.618 --> 00:15:12.620
So I feel like this is
super universal now.

00:15:12.703 --> 00:15:15.123
Anyone can walk in
and envision themselves. I love it.

00:15:15.206 --> 00:15:18.543
I love it, too. I mean, it could've been
done last week, but I love it.

00:15:19.460 --> 00:15:20.753
Let's go upstairs.

00:15:25.091 --> 00:15:27.135
Perfect, I love it.

00:15:28.177 --> 00:15:30.138
[Brett] This could be my bedroom.
I really like it.

00:15:30.221 --> 00:15:32.306
-See the view?
-Yeah, let's go outside.

00:15:35.226 --> 00:15:37.061
[Heather] 
So private up here, don't you think?

00:15:37.311 --> 00:15:39.439
-Yeah, this is great.
-Oh, it's beautiful.

00:15:39.522 --> 00:15:42.316
-[Brett] You'll sell the shit out of this.
-Yay! I hope.

00:15:42.400 --> 00:15:43.818
-You will.
-It's gonna happen quick.

00:15:43.901 --> 00:15:45.361
-It's got to.
-Yeah. You will.

00:15:45.445 --> 00:15:47.447
I got my license when I was 27,

00:15:47.530 --> 00:15:51.492
and literally a few months later,
I sold my first home,

00:15:51.576 --> 00:15:54.078
which was, like, around 7.2 million.

00:15:54.454 --> 00:15:57.915
For me to have to <i>prove</i>
that I am a good agent

00:15:57.999 --> 00:16:01.169
