00:19:04.101 --> 00:19:06.270
This is the television.

00:19:07.063 --> 00:19:08.105
Boom!

00:19:08.189 --> 00:19:10.608
[Mary] That is epic.

00:19:10.691 --> 00:19:12.360
Where'd you guys get that idea?

00:19:12.443 --> 00:19:16.030
-Oh, just in my head one night.
-[Jhoiey] He's crazy sometimes.

00:19:16.113 --> 00:19:18.074
Eighty-five-inch TV right in front.

00:19:18.157 --> 00:19:20.159
[Mary] That is so cool. 
That is incredible.

00:19:20.242 --> 00:19:21.869
Yeah. I'm pretty happy with it.

00:19:21.952 --> 00:19:24.163
-How much did that cost to do?
-[laughs]

00:19:24.246 --> 00:19:26.582
Uh, almost 35,000 with everything.

00:19:27.416 --> 00:19:29.043
Your TV cost 35,000? [laughs]

00:19:29.126 --> 00:19:31.045
Well, no, the TV cost 5,000,
but you have to--

00:19:31.128 --> 00:19:33.964
-But the whole TV system cost... Wow.
-You dig down, pour...

00:19:34.048 --> 00:19:36.050
It's basically a safe room down there.

00:19:36.133 --> 00:19:37.635
It's basically a bunker.

00:19:38.511 --> 00:19:39.387
[laughs]

00:19:39.470 --> 00:19:43.349
Now you've got the industrial
kind of thing. Organic.

00:19:43.724 --> 00:19:45.768
Well, the last one we did
was more contemporary,

00:19:45.851 --> 00:19:48.521
but this is more my style: 
one-story vaulted ceilings,

00:19:48.938 --> 00:19:52.733
wood, metal, timeless, more sophisticated.
 I really like it.

00:19:52.817 --> 00:19:54.318
-I love it.
-This is more me.

00:19:54.402 --> 00:19:56.570
So Jason and I used to date,

00:19:56.654 --> 00:19:58.739
and, yeah, that didn't work out.

00:19:58.823 --> 00:20:01.534
I think in most cases,
it's very hard to work with an ex, but...

00:20:02.827 --> 00:20:04.245
it works for us.

00:20:04.328 --> 00:20:07.998
So it's nice to be able to offer
my opinion objectively.

00:20:08.082 --> 00:20:10.251
And then this is gonna be glass.
One piece of glass.

00:20:10.334 --> 00:20:13.337
By the way, 
I believe I told you to do glass there

00:20:13.421 --> 00:20:16.757
-instead of the other thing, didn't I?
-Instead of metal? Yes, you might have.

00:20:16.841 --> 00:20:19.844
And then this is gonna be a neon sign
with my favorite poem.

00:20:19.927 --> 00:20:22.138
So it'll become like a bar vibe over here.

00:20:22.263 --> 00:20:23.180
Here, let's go outside.

00:20:23.723 --> 00:20:25.349
We're just getting started on the pool.

00:20:25.433 --> 00:20:28.894
So the coping goes first and then they're
gonna float everything around that.

00:20:28.978 --> 00:20:32.523
Then all of this is
gonna be fake grass, the entire deck.

00:20:32.732 --> 00:20:35.025
The brick on all the pillars,
are you leaving it brick?

00:20:35.109 --> 00:20:36.360
-Yes.
-Oh, yeah, for sure.

00:20:36.444 --> 00:20:38.070
-Okay.
-It's called thin brick,

00:20:38.154 --> 00:20:39.530
which you'll normally see.

00:20:39.613 --> 00:20:41.866
I hate the word veneer,
'cause everyone thinks it's fake.

00:20:41.949 --> 00:20:43.951
It's actually brick. It's just thin.

00:20:44.034 --> 00:20:46.412
-It;s just the thinner--
-So let's go with thin brick, deal?

00:20:46.495 --> 00:20:47.747
[Jhoiey laughs]

00:20:47.830 --> 00:20:50.916
-He's making up his own words.
-This is gonna be a fireplace

00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:52.585
right here, too, in the corner.

00:20:52.668 --> 00:20:54.170
What's up, guys?

00:20:54.253 --> 00:20:55.212
What's up, girl?

00:20:55.296 --> 00:20:56.130
Hey.

00:20:56.213 --> 00:20:59.592
I was just here and Mary told me
she's going to be here,

00:20:59.675 --> 00:21:01.135
so I figured I'd come say hi.

00:21:01.218 --> 00:21:03.596
-Oh, I wanna brag about the house.
-I know. Wow.

00:21:03.679 --> 00:21:05.514
-Hey, hon. You look cute.
-You look nice too.

00:21:05.598 --> 00:21:07.725
-I love your jumper.
-Oh, thank you.

00:21:07.808 --> 00:21:09.894
-Wow, this is so nice!
-You know Jhoiey, right?

00:21:09.977 --> 00:21:12.396
I'm sorry, I got distracted. Maya.

00:21:12.480 --> 00:21:15.941
Oh, by the way, we're gonna have a huge
pool party/dinner party when I'm done.

00:21:16.025 --> 00:21:17.026
When is it gonna be ready?

00:21:17.193 --> 00:21:19.278
I don't know.
Jhoiey, when's it gonna be ready?

00:21:19.528 --> 00:21:21.822
-The pressure is on.
-Uh-oh, here comes another fight.

00:21:21.947 --> 00:21:24.283
[Jason] We're gonna go inside.
We have a ton to go over.

00:21:24.366 --> 00:21:25.993
-Nice to meet you.
-Nice to meet you, too.

00:21:26.327 --> 00:21:27.578
[Maya] What's going on, girl?

00:21:27.661 --> 00:21:30.581
[Mary] Nothing. Just coming to the house
to take a look a look at it.

00:21:30.664 --> 00:21:32.374
He's just, like, done so much to it.

00:21:32.458 --> 00:21:35.920
I was here a couple months ago
and it just looks completely different.

00:21:36.170 --> 00:21:38.047
It's the first time I see it. I like it.

00:21:38.130 --> 00:21:39.298
So how have you been?

00:21:39.381 --> 00:21:40.257
-Good! 
-Yeah?

00:21:40.341 --> 00:21:43.427
-Yeah, really good. Yeah.
-What's going on with you and Romain?

00:21:43.511 --> 00:21:46.847
I know it's been kind of like, 
you know, the girls are, like,

00:21:46.931 --> 00:21:50.601
chit-chatting in the office and making,
I guess, some comments about,

00:21:50.684 --> 00:21:53.646
-you know, him being young and--
-Who was talking about stuff?

00:21:53.896 --> 00:21:56.732
I guess, I don't know, Davina
and Chrishell were, like, talking about,

00:21:56.816 --> 00:22:00.402
you know, I wonder if, like, you are,
like, supporting him or something.

00:22:00.486 --> 00:22:02.988
But I get it, people talk.
They will always say something.

00:22:03.072 --> 00:22:04.281
Yeah.

00:22:04.490 --> 00:22:08.452
Well, I don't support him at all,

00:22:08.536 --> 00:22:11.914
but if they have questions, if they have
something to say, they can just ask me.

00:22:11.997 --> 00:22:13.499
What... Was there anything else said?

00:22:13.749 --> 00:22:16.544
-No. That's what, as far as I know.
-Okay.

00:22:16.627 --> 00:22:18.379
If they want to know,
they can come to me.

00:22:18.462 --> 00:22:20.506
-Right.
-They don't need to talk behind my back.

00:22:22.299 --> 00:22:27.012
<i>♪ I hope my fears don't catch me ♪</i>

00:22:28.013 --> 00:22:34.061
<i>♪ And you won't see me when I fall ♪</i>

00:22:34.144 --> 00:22:37.439
[Chrishell] Do any of you guys have 
an agent that works in Vegas?

00:22:37.523 --> 00:22:38.858
-I do.
-I need a referral.

00:22:38.941 --> 00:22:40.067
[Heather] Yeah.

00:22:40.359 --> 00:22:41.402
It's from ten to two.

00:22:41.485 --> 00:22:43.988
Are we still going 
to the Century next week?

00:22:44.071 --> 00:22:46.448
-Wasn't there something--
-I have to talk to Eric about that.

00:22:46.532 --> 00:22:47.533
All right.

00:22:47.616 --> 00:22:51.579
-Hey. Sorry, um, do you have a second?
-Yeah, go ahead.

00:22:52.079 --> 00:22:56.000
So, unfortunately, um,
remember the last time I told you

00:22:56.083 --> 00:22:57.793
they had an offer in, we're in escrow,

00:22:57.877 --> 00:22:59.879
but it was contingent
on their house selling?

00:22:59.962 --> 00:23:01.255
-On the Encino property?
-Yeah.

00:23:01.547 --> 00:23:04.258
So we're basically to the point now

00:23:04.341 --> 00:23:08.846
where their deposit would be at risk and 
they've taken their offer off the table

00:23:08.929 --> 00:23:10.931
'cause they're afraid
their house is not gonna sell.

00:23:11.515 --> 00:23:13.809
-So my escrow fell through.
-Hmm.

00:23:14.393 --> 00:23:16.186
[Jason] Well, where's the backup offer?

00:23:16.270 --> 00:23:18.105
Well, this is the only offer I have.

00:23:18.188 --> 00:23:19.732
Well, we need a backup offer.

00:23:19.815 --> 00:23:22.484
If you think that there's an escrow
that could fall out,

00:23:22.568 --> 00:23:25.863
then you gotta have a backup offer,
maybe even an offer before that.

00:23:25.946 --> 00:23:27.907
Two backup offers. 
I don't wanna hear

00:23:27.990 --> 00:23:30.868
you coming to me saying I lost
an escrow and I don't have a backup offer.

00:23:31.285 --> 00:23:32.870
Did you continue to have open houses

00:23:32.953 --> 00:23:35.956
and broker opens and continue to make
phone calls and send out emails

00:23:36.040 --> 00:23:39.460
and do print marketing? If you can get
one offer, you can get two offers.

00:23:39.543 --> 00:23:42.463
Okay. I did show the house privately
a couple times,

00:23:42.546 --> 00:23:44.924
but I didn't hold it open
after I was in escrow, but--

00:23:45.007 --> 00:23:48.218
You gotta keep working. 
I mean what, you lost your first deal?

00:23:48.302 --> 00:23:50.846
-Not a good batting average.
-[Chrishell] Well...

00:23:50.930 --> 00:23:53.682
[Jason] I mean, I lose maybe one
in every 20 or 30 deals.

00:23:53.766 --> 00:23:57.770
Well, then maybe this is just my one
and I'm getting it out of the way,

00:23:57.853 --> 00:23:59.939
and then all the rest of them
will be real successful.

00:24:00.022 --> 00:24:02.775
I don't want you coming back
and saying, "I fell out of escrow

00:24:02.858 --> 00:24:05.694
and I don't have a backup offer
because I didn't continue to work hard."

00:24:05.778 --> 00:24:07.613
I did show it privately a couple times--

00:24:07.696 --> 00:24:09.823
Because now 
the client's not happy with us, right?

00:24:09.907 --> 00:24:12.618
Because you got them excited,
they felt like they sold the house,

00:24:12.701 --> 00:24:16.163
they might've made plans to, you know,
move or spend that money or do something,

00:24:16.246 --> 00:24:18.207
and now, boom, we're back to square one.

00:24:18.290 --> 00:24:20.876
I mean, listen, I'm not just gonna
judge you on one deal,

00:24:20.960 --> 00:24:23.045
but, you know, it's not a great start.

00:24:23.629 --> 00:24:26.590
All right. I'm going to hold it open
on Sunday, Tuesday.

00:24:26.674 --> 00:24:30.052
I'll blast emails out. I'll call
some people that did come to see it,

00:24:30.135 --> 00:24:31.845
to make sure they know
it's still available.

00:24:31.929 --> 00:24:34.640
Let's get our marketing back.
Let's get people back to the house.

00:24:34.723 --> 00:24:36.433
All right. Sorry. Thank you.

00:24:36.517 --> 00:24:39.645
Let's get an ad in the LA Times,
get an ad in the MLS Caravan.

00:24:39.728 --> 00:24:41.522
The whole team can send emails.
Tell everybody.

00:24:41.605 --> 00:24:42.815
-Okay.
-All right.

00:24:42.898 --> 00:24:43.857
Thank you.

00:24:47.152 --> 00:24:49.571
You guys have anybody that's looking
to move to the Valley?

00:24:49.655 --> 00:24:51.907
-[Maya] What happened?
-[Chrishell] I fell out of escrow.

00:24:51.991 --> 00:24:55.035
What happened is that she fell out
of escrow on her deal

00:24:55.119 --> 00:24:56.662
because she didn't have a backup offer.

00:24:56.745 --> 00:24:59.540
We're back to square one.
So, lesson for everyone,

00:24:59.623 --> 00:25:01.625
if they don't know this,
and I think everyone does,

00:25:01.709 --> 00:25:04.378
use your first offer
to get a backup offer.

00:25:04.461 --> 00:25:05.963
[Heather] It's not your fault.

00:25:06.046 --> 00:25:08.924
If you don't have a backup offer,
you can't wait around for a backup offer.

00:25:09.008 --> 00:25:11.343
Well, it <i>is</i> her fault, actually,

00:25:11.427 --> 00:25:13.887
but, you know, you could've had
a couple more open houses.

00:25:14.138 --> 00:25:16.265
You can go and sit
next to Jason, Christine.

00:25:16.348 --> 00:25:19.393
[Christine] I'm just saying it happens. 
It's okay. She knows now.

00:25:19.476 --> 00:25:20.310
It's not a perfect world

00:25:20.394 --> 00:25:22.438
and not everyone has
a backup offer for every listing.

00:25:22.521 --> 00:25:24.314
[Christine] But she knows now
that she should.

00:25:24.398 --> 00:25:27.401
You know, you're the one that's 
missing out on a six-figure commission,

00:25:27.484 --> 00:25:29.111
so I'm not trying to be the bad guy here,

00:25:29.820 --> 00:25:31.905
but, you know, 
you're batting zero right now

00:25:31.989 --> 00:25:36.243
so let's close maybe our next 15 deals
and then you'll be back to average.

00:25:37.411 --> 00:25:38.954
Don't worry, like, it happens.

00:25:43.083 --> 00:25:45.461
<i>♪ High, is it what you want? ♪</i>

00:25:45.544 --> 00:25:49.298
<i>♪ Taking me, breaking me</i>
<i>Getting me high ♪</i>

00:25:49.381 --> 00:25:50.549
♪ <i>Is it what you want? </i>♪

00:25:50.632 --> 00:25:52.468
<i>♪ Touching me ♪</i>

00:25:53.427 --> 00:25:55.804
<i>♪ High, is what you want? ♪</i>

00:25:55.888 --> 00:25:57.806
♪ <i>Work it with me </i>♪

00:25:57.890 --> 00:26:00.559
[Maya] Wow, what a long day, ladies.
[sighs wearily]

00:26:03.854 --> 00:26:06.315
Oh, this is so nice.
Have you guys been here before?

00:26:06.398 --> 00:26:09.485
-I have, but only downstairs.
-[Christine] Yeah? It's super cute.

00:26:09.568 --> 00:26:13.655
You know, it's nice to finally escape
from Jason and Brett. [chuckles]

00:26:14.073 --> 00:26:16.492
Are they gonna show up from nowhere?
Like, they always show up.

00:26:16.575 --> 00:26:18.243
-Probably!
-[woman] Hi, ladies.

00:26:18.327 --> 00:26:21.205
Welcome to the District, I'll be helping
you out tonight, my name's Chanel.

00:26:21.288 --> 00:26:22.998
I'll start with your drinks?

00:26:23.082 --> 00:26:25.459
-Sauv blanc. Great, thank you.
-[Chanel] Yeah, definitely.

00:26:25.542 --> 00:26:27.711
-Would you wanna do a New Zealand one?
-Wonderful.

00:26:27.795 --> 00:26:29.797
-[Chanel] Okay, for yourself?
-Could I have a mojito.

00:26:29.880 --> 00:26:30.881
[Chanel] Mojito.

00:26:31.757 --> 00:26:33.967
-I'll do a champagne.
-Champagne.

00:26:34.426 --> 00:26:36.011
-Mojito.
-And a mojito.

00:26:36.095 --> 00:26:38.097
-A virgin one.
-Virgin.

00:26:38.180 --> 00:26:39.807
[Christine] Four lemon drop shots, please.

00:26:40.349 --> 00:26:42.726
-[Chanel] Sounds good. Thank you.
-Thank you.

00:26:43.852 --> 00:26:46.480
Now we need to just work
on the 40-million-dollar houses.

00:26:46.563 --> 00:26:47.940
I know!

00:26:48.023 --> 00:26:51.026
I feel like my client, in his mind,
that wasn't even when he wanted.

00:26:51.110 --> 00:26:51.985
-Jacob?
-Yeah.

00:26:52.069 --> 00:26:54.238
-This is the guy that--
-Oh, my gosh.

00:26:54.321 --> 00:26:56.115
-Yes, this is <i>the</i> Jacob.
-Okay.

00:26:56.198 --> 00:26:58.367
-Cheers. Thank you.
-I'll grab some waters as well.

00:26:58.450 --> 00:27:00.494
-Thank you. Cheers, ladies!
-Of course.

00:27:00.577 --> 00:27:03.413
Cheers, guys.

00:27:04.540 --> 00:27:06.166
-Yeah. Cheers.
-Cheers.

00:27:06.250 --> 00:27:08.710
So I had buyers like that, actually.

00:27:10.170 --> 00:27:12.840
Well, I have a question: you haven't
talked to him since the flowers?

00:27:12.923 --> 00:27:14.007
Like, in person?

00:27:14.091 --> 00:27:15.801
No, I haven't seen him since the flowers.

00:27:15.884 --> 00:27:18.595
-[Chrishell] Could I see a picture of him?
-So here we go.

00:27:18.679 --> 00:27:19.680
Yes!

00:27:20.222 --> 00:27:21.765
Oh, he looks sexy.

00:27:21.849 --> 00:27:24.309
Wait, I wanna see him.
I'm missing all the action.

00:27:24.393 --> 00:27:26.061
-[cell phone rings]
-[gasps]

00:27:26.145 --> 00:27:27.146
[laughs]

00:27:27.229 --> 00:27:28.188
[Maya] Who is that?

00:27:28.272 --> 00:27:29.523
Can I answer? Can I get it?

00:27:29.731 --> 00:27:31.984
-Oh, that's Jacob.
-No, I'm busy.

00:27:32.067 --> 00:27:33.819
Why? Let me answer!

00:27:33.902 --> 00:27:35.904
I can't talk to him right now. I can't.

00:27:35.988 --> 00:27:38.240
He's like my brother,
do you know what I mean?

00:27:38.323 --> 00:27:40.576
It's like, I don't know,
I've known him since, like...

00:27:40.659 --> 00:27:41.493
[Maya] Yeah.

00:27:41.577 --> 00:27:43.120
[Chanel] Some lemon drop shots.

00:27:43.203 --> 00:27:45.622
[Chrishell] Oh! Thank you.

00:27:49.001 --> 00:27:49.960
All right, cheers.

00:27:50.043 --> 00:27:52.379
-I'm not--
-[Christine] You gonna do it?

00:27:52.462 --> 00:27:54.339
To the baby! [laughs]

00:27:55.382 --> 00:27:57.009
-I'm sorry, Maya.
-That--

00:27:57.092 --> 00:27:58.969
I'm kidding! I'm joking.

00:27:59.052 --> 00:28:00.596
Why are you not drinking?

00:28:01.597 --> 00:28:03.557
Well, I'm basically pregnant, ... it.

00:28:03.640 --> 00:28:05.434
Good job, Chrishell. [chuckles]

00:28:05.517 --> 00:28:07.561
-I forgot. I'm sorry.
-It's very early.

00:28:07.644 --> 00:28:09.646
-Basically pregnant or you're pregnant?
-Well, I am.

00:28:09.855 --> 00:28:14.151
-I am, but it's, like, so... It's fine.
-This is why I can't drink! I'm sorry.

00:28:14.401 --> 00:28:16.195
This is great, though. This is great news.

00:28:16.278 --> 00:28:20.407
It's great, but I just hope it's gonna,
you know, stay, right?

00:28:20.490 --> 00:28:21.825
So that's why I'm like...

00:28:21.909 --> 00:28:23.660
I'm so sorry!

00:28:25.913 --> 00:28:28.540
One sip of alcohol,
this one is already like...

00:28:28.665 --> 00:28:29.750
[Davina] Done. Toast.

00:28:29.833 --> 00:28:31.210
[Maya] Seriously.

00:28:31.293 --> 00:28:35.047
Try to not tell Mary and Heather
or something? Or just keep it kind of--

00:28:35.130 --> 00:28:38.800
I better not drink then because...
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.

00:28:53.732 --> 00:28:55.150
Hi, babe!

00:28:55.234 --> 00:28:57.694
-Hey!
-Hi, guys. How are you?

00:28:57.778 --> 00:28:59.613
Hi, honey.

00:28:59.696 --> 00:29:01.323
-You look cute.
-Thank you.

00:29:01.406 --> 00:29:03.450
-Come on in. 
-You need a drink.

00:29:03.533 --> 00:29:05.911
We have a few extra lemon drops
if you'd like one.

00:29:05.994 --> 00:29:06.954
Ooh!

00:29:07.496 --> 00:29:08.914
[Maya] So how was your day?

00:29:08.997 --> 00:29:11.959
It was all right. 
I just did a walk through with a client,

00:29:12.042 --> 00:29:14.920
and, um, it was kind of a disaster, but...

00:29:15.170 --> 00:29:16.380
Oh, no, what happened?

00:29:16.463 --> 00:29:17.631
It didn't go as...

00:29:17.714 --> 00:29:22.261
So basically the seller moved out
and just left it a mess,

00:29:22.344 --> 00:29:27.766
so I was trying to, like, scurry and 
clean everything up and stuff and...

00:29:27.849 --> 00:29:30.477
It's much more responsibility
representing the buyer and the seller

00:29:30.560 --> 00:29:33.397
because you're, you know,
at fault for everything, literally.

00:29:33.480 --> 00:29:36.692
Yeah, that's true. But you also make,
like, a lot more money.

00:29:36.775 --> 00:29:38.777
[Christine] Yeah, that's true.
Absolutely true.

00:29:38.944 --> 00:29:41.071
-Yes, but I did find it--
-[Christine] So Mary's buying.

00:29:41.863 --> 00:29:44.116
-Drinks on Mary. [chuckles]
-[Davina] Drinks on Mary!

00:29:44.199 --> 00:29:45.075
[Mary] Oh, my gosh.

00:29:45.534 --> 00:29:48.620
-Um... oh. So...
-[Davina] That's funny.

00:29:48.704 --> 00:29:50.622
I'm just going to get this out, like,

00:29:51.206 --> 00:29:55.752
in the open right away 
because I did speak to Maya the other day

00:29:56.128 --> 00:29:57.546
and she just said that...

00:29:58.380 --> 00:30:03.218
there was some talk 
about Romain and my relationship.

00:30:03.468 --> 00:30:06.596
To be honest, I heard, 
like, you guys were talking.

00:30:06.680 --> 00:30:08.890
But here's the thing: you guys are new.

00:30:10.225 --> 00:30:13.979
How would you know anything about us?

00:30:14.271 --> 00:30:17.649
I do want to make it clear
he's never asked me for a penny.

00:30:17.733 --> 00:30:19.735
He pays for the two of us all the time.

00:30:19.818 --> 00:30:23.405
It's frustrating that people are talking--

00:30:23.488 --> 00:30:24.656
I swear to God,

00:30:24.740 --> 00:30:26.074
I don't remember.

00:30:27.117 --> 00:30:29.703
You did ask me about,
like, does he pay for stuff?

00:30:29.786 --> 00:30:33.248
Yeah. And it's... I think it's because
you don't really know, you know?

00:30:33.832 --> 00:30:34.750
Okay.

00:30:38.211 --> 00:30:39.921
I'm gonna use the restroom.

00:30:40.088 --> 00:30:42.591
-[Maya] Me, too. I have to pee, too.
-Crazy. I do, too.

00:30:46.053 --> 00:30:48.972
You threw me under the bus to Mary
about that I asked,

00:30:49.723 --> 00:30:52.017
like, if she paid for everything.

00:30:52.100 --> 00:30:55.479
I was only asking because 
I legitimately was wondering

00:30:55.562 --> 00:30:56.980
why there was all this concern.

00:30:57.147 --> 00:31:00.233
[Davina] Well, I feel like she does know
that it was, like, about the kids

00:31:00.317 --> 00:31:01.318
and about the money.

00:31:01.401 --> 00:31:03.528
So those are the two general points
and you're like,

00:31:03.612 --> 00:31:05.197
"For me, it was only about the kids."

00:31:05.280 --> 00:31:09.785
Then I'm the one that obviously was
talking this shit about, uh, the money.

00:31:09.868 --> 00:31:12.245
So I was like, "That's not the case,"
and so I feel because--

00:31:12.329 --> 00:31:15.540
-So then you threw it on me.
-No. Maya's the one that told Mary,

00:31:15.624 --> 00:31:17.459
"Oh, you know, 
they were talking about it."

00:31:17.542 --> 00:31:20.379
So it's not like I was like,
"Hey, Mary, uh, by the way,

00:31:20.462 --> 00:31:22.756
this is what was talked about,"
you know? So just know that.

00:31:22.839 --> 00:31:26.551
The way that you 
brought it up to Mary sounded like

00:31:26.635 --> 00:31:28.595
you were throwing me under the bus--

00:31:28.678 --> 00:31:30.222
But you could've owned up to it

00:31:30.305 --> 00:31:34.684
and said, "Oh, actually, I don't know him.
I don't know you very well."

00:31:34.768 --> 00:31:36.728
And that's the reality of the situation.

00:31:37.312 --> 00:31:38.730
Uh... Really?

00:31:39.106 --> 00:31:42.484
It's just letting me know
who I can trust, who I can't.

00:31:45.821 --> 00:31:46.947
Did you get your fried rice?

00:31:47.406 --> 00:31:49.533
-[Maya] Yes. You want some?
-[Mary] Nah.

00:31:50.409 --> 00:31:53.620
<i>♪ Just another day in paradise ♪</i>

00:31:53.703 --> 00:31:55.163
<i>♪ A day in paradise </i>♪

00:31:55.247 --> 00:31:58.041
♪ <i>Another day in paradise </i>♪